# =============================================================================
# .trivyignore — Trivy CVE Allowlist for Backend Image
# Project: Final DevOps - Phase 3
# Purpose: Whitelist identified CVEs based on risk assessment for runtime environment.
# Last Reviewed: 2026-05-06 | Team DevOps
# =============================================================================

# --- Package: cross-spawn ---
# CVE-2024-21538: Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS)
# Justification: The backend does not spawn processes using unsanitized user input.
# Mitigation: Input validation and sanitization are enforced at the API gateway.
CVE-2024-21538

# --- Package: glob ---
# CVE-2025-64756: Command Injection Vulnerability via Malicious Filenames
# Justification: Application logic does not use glob patterns on user-controllable filenames.
# Mitigation: Awaiting compatibility testing for version 11.1.0 upgrade.
CVE-2025-64756

# --- Package: minimatch ---
# CVE-2026-26996, CVE-2026-27903, CVE-2026-27904: Denial of Service via glob patterns
# Justification: These are build-time dependencies used for file matching during CI/CD.
# Mitigation: Not exposed to external traffic or runtime request handling.
CVE-2026-26996
CVE-2026-27903
CVE-2026-27904

# --- Package: tar ---
# CVE-2026-23745, CVE-2026-23950, CVE-2026-24842: Arbitrary file overwrite
# CVE-2026-26960, CVE-2026-29786, CVE-2026-31802: Path traversal/Hardlink poisoning
# Justification: The application does not perform extraction of untrusted tar archives.
# Mitigation: Container runs with restricted filesystem permissions and non-root user.
CVE-2026-23745
CVE-2026-23950
CVE-2026-24842
CVE-2026-26960
CVE-2026-29786
CVE-2026-31802